<headroom-library version="1" id="hg-tampa-death-rhythm" category="High Gain" order="80" instrument="guitar" style="Death Metal">
  <description>Thick, mid-heavy Florida death metal rhythm: an op-amp distortion used as a dark push into a rectified high-gain head with the mids up, into a 4x12. Close, dense and growling, with the low mids that make tremolo riffs and slow, crushing parts sound enormous.</description>
  <tags><tag>High Gain</tag><tag>Death Metal</tag><tag>Florida</tag><tag>Rhythm</tag><tag>Mid-Heavy</tag><tag>Gate</tag><tag>Downtuned</tag></tags>
  <sources>
    <source url="https://www.guitarworld.com/features/obituary-trevor-peres-ken-andrews-dying-of-everything" title="Guitar World: Obituary's Trevor Peres and Ken Andrews"/>
    <source url="https://www.decibelmagazine.com/2023/09/11/pre-order-the-scott-burns-sessions-a-life-in-death-metal-1987-1997-from-decibel-books-read-an-exclusive-excerpt-now/" title="Decibel: The Scott Burns Sessions, book excerpt"/>
    <source url="https://tapeop.com/interviews/173/scott-burns" title="Tape Op: Scott Burns interview"/>
    <source url="https://www.musicradar.com/news/5-songs-guitar-players-Death" title="MusicRadar: Death, five songs guitar players need to hear"/>
  </sources>
</headroom-library>
